WEBVTT

00:00:56.227 --> 00:01:00.397
Nobody wants to hear you cry 
about the grief inside your bones

00:01:00.397 --> 00:01:01.718
But my bones said

00:01:01.718 --> 00:01:07.238
“Tyler Clementi dove into the Hudson River
convinced he was entirely alone.”

00:01:07.238 --> 00:01:10.551
My bones said “write the poem.”

00:01:10.551 --> 00:01:11.798
To the lamplight.

00:01:11.798 --> 00:01:13.097
Considering the river bed.

00:01:13.097 --> 00:01:16.426
To the chandelier of your fate hanging by a thread.

00:01:16.426 --> 00:01:18.855
To everyday you could not get out of bed.

00:01:18.855 --> 00:01:20.718
To the bulls eye of your wrist

00:01:20.718 --> 00:01:23.167
To anyone who has ever wanted to die.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:26.647
I have been told, sometimes, 
the most healing thing we can do-

00:01:26.647 --> 00:01:29.717
Is remind ourselves over and over and over

00:01:29.717 --> 00:01:31.888
Other people feel this too